.TH CIGAR 1 "2026-07-12" "CIGAR 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cigar \- deterministic context, coordination, effect, and replay client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cigar
[global options] command [subcommand] [resource-id]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CIGAR compiles each API-backed command into the frozen operation identifier
and canonical request envelope.
Mutations require explicit confirmation and support dry run.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --output " text|json"
Select human or versioned JSON output.
.TP
.BI --deadline " Nms|Ns|Nm"
Bound the complete operation.
.TP
.BI --target " embedded|local|remote"
Select an explicit execution target.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate and authorize a mutation without committing it.
.TP
.B --yes
Confirm a reviewed state change.
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Disable prompting; unconfirmed mutations fail.
.TP
.B --security
Run the bounded local security checks supported by
.BR doctor .
.TP
.B --deep
Run the complete content-integrity and projection checks supported by
.BR doctor .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize atomic local administration state.
.TP
.B source add|list|refresh|inspect|remove
Manage local CLI source references and run frozen production discovery/status
operations.
.TP
.B ingest
Ingest an accepted discovery plan.
.TP
.B status
Report structured target readiness.
.TP
.B context plan|compile|explain|diff|revalidate|materialize
Plan, compile, compare, explain, validate, or materialize context.
.TP
.B project list|attach|detach|switch|link|unlink
Manage project eligibility and explicit disclosure links.
.TP
.B focus new|switch|checkpoint|close
Manage the active context space.
.TP
.B space fork|publish|log|conflicts
Operate and inspect durable context spaces.
.TP
.B handoff create|preview|inspect|accept|revoke|merge
Operate governed handoff capsules.
.TP
.B effect prepare|approve|dispatch|list|inspect|reconcile|compensate
Operate the durable effect journal.
Dispatch and compensation require confirmation.
.TP
.B replay reconstruct|run|compare|completeness
Reconstruct and evaluate replay jobs.
.TP
.B policy check|explain
Evaluate or explain the explicit local production policy profile.
.TP
.B backup create|verify|restore
Create or verify a signed production archive, or restore it to an explicit
empty target.
Create and verify take one archive path; restore takes the archive and target
paths.
.TP
.B gc plan|run
Plan or execute bounded, repository-owned encrypted-blob mark-and-sweep.
Physical deletion requires a versioned JSON policy document proving expired
retention and replay windows, no legal hold, a completed backup policy, and a
positive bounded file limit.
.TP
.BI "diagnostics bundle " archive
Create a deterministic, content-free support archive containing only bounded
build, configuration, platform, inventory, and diagnostic metadata.
.TP
.B doctor [--security] [--deep]
Report actionable component diagnostics. Security mode validates protected
local configuration and durable-store settings; deep mode additionally verifies
retained snapshots, journals, blobs, indexes, and exact SQL and full-text
projections without emitting stored content.
.TP
.B serve
Run the installed daemon with the configured production file.
.TP
.B mcp serve
Run the installed stdio MCP adapter.
.TP
.B plugin install|uninstall|doctor claude-code
Preview, install, remove, or diagnose the user-scoped Claude Code adapter
through documented Claude plugin commands. Uninstall preserves portable CIGAR
catalog data.
.TP
.B release verify
Delegate offline release verification to the authoritative installed task.
.SH SECURITY
Authorization material is read from a bounded regular file and is never emitted.
JSON errors contain only stable public codes, messages, and remediation.
.SH SEE ALSO
cigard(1)
